292	    /**
293	     * Whether the owner's tenure — the number of elapsed fiscal years from the registration date to
294	     * the current server date — exceeds one year (strictly more than one elapsed fiscal year). The
295	     * elapsed count is the difference between the fiscal year of the current server date and the
296	     * fiscal year of the registration date. This gates the top membership level: only an owner past
297	     * a full year of tenure can reach level 4. A {@code null} registration date counts as zero
298	     * tenure and so never exceeds the threshold, which is why a newly created owner (zero tenure)
299	     * can never exceed level 3.
300	     *
301	     * @param registrationDate the date the owner registered, or {@code null} when absent
302	     * @return {@code true} when more than one fiscal year has elapsed since registration
303	     */
304	    public static boolean tenureExceedsOneYear(LocalDate registrationDate) {
305	        if (registrationDate == null) {
306	            return false;
307	        }
308	        return fiscalYearNumber(LocalDate.now()) - fiscalYearNumber(registrationDate) > 1;
309	    }
